<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.tradingbotapp.ftmo</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-lc</string>
        <string>/Users/kaloyanivanov/TradingBotApp/ftmo_runner.sh</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Install with:
             cp com.tradingbotapp.ftmo.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
             launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.tradingbotapp.ftmo.plist
             launchctl load   ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.tradingbotapp.ftmo.plist
         Verify UNSANDBOXED with `launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.tradingbotapp.ftmo`
         — a bare `launchctl list` from an agent shell reports a different
         domain and will show a loaded job as missing.

         WAKES EVERY 15 MINUTES, EVERY HOUR, EVERY DAY (:00 :15 :30 :45).
         Changed 2026-08-11 from hourly at :30.

         This schedule is a deliberate SUPERSET and is NOT the trading window.
         The window — 16:30 to 23:00 Europe/Sofia, MONDAY TO FRIDAY, i.e. the
         09:30-16:00 New York cash session (owner decision 2026-08-11) — is
         enforced by `ftmo_runner.within_trading_window()`, and THAT is
         authoritative. 27 of the 96 daily wakeups are in-window on a weekday
         and none are at the weekend.

         Note the entries omit <key>Hour</key> deliberately. An unspecified
         StartCalendarInterval field is a WILDCARD, so four dicts express
         "every hour at these four minutes" — where naming the hours would
         take 96. The previous version listed 24 explicit hours; this is the
         same idea with the wildcard doing the work.

         Why the window itself is still not encoded here. A plist is expressed
         in whatever the host's local timezone happens to be, whereas the
         runner resolves `Europe/Sofia` through zoneinfo and therefore stays
         right across the EEST/EET switch and across any change to the
         machine's own timezone. The retired IBKR runner split NYSE hours the
         same way and for the same reason: the plist only has to be a
         superset, the code decides.

         Out-of-window wakeups are free by construction — the runner checks
         the window before opening the audit log and long before importing
         torch, so a wakeup outside the session costs one settings read.

         OVERLAPPING RUNS. A full cycle takes ~6.3 minutes on the 101-symbol
         universe against a 15-minute interval, so a slow run could still be
         going when the next one starts. `ftmo_runner.py` takes a PID lock and
         a second concurrent firing exits immediately. This is not theoretical:
         on 2026-08-11 two concurrent runners each loaded their own ~2 GB
         Kronos model, the machine went into swap, and the unattended firing
         was left with 28 seconds of CPU across 13 minutes of wall clock.

         The FTMO day boundary (00:00 Europe/Prague) falls at 01:00 Sofia,
         which is now OUTSIDE the trading window. `advance_state()` therefore
         rolls the day-start balance on the FIRST IN-WINDOW FIRING of the new
         FTMO day — 16:30 Sofia — rather than at 01:30 as it did under the
         old overnight window. It rolls off the previous day's settled closing
         balance either way; only the moment of discovery moved.

         FTMO's 23:55-00:05 Moscow maintenance window is deliberately NOT
         scheduled around. The venue stays the authority: a MARKET_CLOSED
         rejection is journalled and the run ends without placing anything,
         which is the correct outcome rather than something to predict. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>15</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>45</integer></dict>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/kaloyanivanov/TradingBotApp/ftmo_launchd.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/kaloyanivanov/TradingBotApp/ftmo_launchd.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
